{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":45},"timestamp":1790173571,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":".venv/bin/cortex-ask --real --tenant █████████ \"which stage are we losing the most deals at, by █████ and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\"","title":"real_where_deals_die","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: which stage are we losing the most deals at, by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-23 19:56:12\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.0s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  1.0s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  1.0s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  1.0s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  1.0s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [  5.1s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 12.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 12.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 12.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__pipeline\r\n  [ 14.6s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 14.6s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 14.6s] step 1   got hubspot__pipeline (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 14.6s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 17.7s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588\u2588 rows) (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 17.7s] step 2   got read hubspot.pipeline in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 17.7s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 48.7s]          drafting the report from 6 observation(s)\r\n  [113.9s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [114.0s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (5.5s); missing: Stage-level breakdown of closed-lost deals (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed by the stage they were in prior to being marked closedlost), not just the aggregate closedlost list; Full record set for closed-lost deals rather than 100 of 218 truncated results; Historical stage-loss comparison across an earlier period to know if this distribution is a change or baseline; Deal history/timeline data showing which pipeline stage each lost deal was sitting in before loss\r\n  [130.9s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Which stage are we losing the most deals at, by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 114s over 3 steps, 67,698 tokens, 6 observations gathered, 3 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The question as asked cannot be answered directly: closed-lost deals in this CRM are recorded only with a terminal stage of 'closedlost', with no property capturing which funnel stage the deal was in before it was lost, across all \u2588\u2588\u2588 lost deals in the trailing \u2588\u2588 months.  [hubspot.search dd14c96f]\r\n  Over the period, \u2588\u2588\u2588 deals closed lost against only \u2588\u2588 closed won ($\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 total won), and a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 share of the lost records cluster around a single bulk-creation date (2026-01-05) with null amount and owner, suggesting much of the lost \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 is a legacy backfill rather than live-pipeline attrition.  [hubspot.search dd14c96f, hubspot.closed_won 26c8926f]\r\n  The immediate fix is process, not analysis: start recording the stage a deal occupies at the moment it is marked lost, so this question is answerable going forward.  [hubspot.search dd14c96f]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Deal loss is not attributable to a specific pipeline stage in this CRM data  (high)\r\n    - Every one of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 deals closed-lost in the trailing \u2588\u2588 months is recorded with stage value 'closedlost' only; the property that would show the stage occupied before loss does not exist in these records.  [hubspot.search dd14c96f]\r\n  Losses vastly outnumber wins over the period, but a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 share of the loss \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 looks like a one-time backlog import rather than live churn  (medium)\r\n    - Over the same \u2588\u2588 months, \u2588\u2588\u2588 deals closed lost versus only \u2588\u2588 closed won, a roughly \u2588\u2588:\u2588 loss-to-win ratio by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588.  [hubspot.search dd14c96f, hubspot.closed_won 26c8926f]\r\n    - Won deals total $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across \u2588\u2588 deals (avg ~$\u2588\u2588\u2588k); the sampled \u2588\u2588\u2588 lost deals with a recorded amount sum to $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across only \u2588\u2588 of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 rows, with the other \u2588\u2588 having no amount recorded at all.  [hubspot.closed_won 26c8926f, hubspot.search dd14c96f]\r\n    - A \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 cluster of the lost records \u2014 dozens of rows with created_at timestamped 2026-01-05, no owner, no amount, and generic '\u2588\u2588\u2588'/'Self-hosted'/'SaaS' placeholder names \u2014 look like a bulk historical import rather than deals that moved through the live pipeline and were actively lost.  [hubspot.search dd14c96f]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] Most deal value is being lost at the qualification or \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 stage, before a proposal is even presented.\r\n      This cannot be tested because closed-lost records do not retain the stage the deal occupied prior to loss; every lost record simply shows stage='closedlost'. No observation available distinguishes an \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-stage loss from a late-stage loss.\r\n  [inconclusive] The high \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of closed-lost deals (\u2588\u2588\u2588) is inflated by a one-time bulk data import dated 2026-01-05 rather than reflecting an ongoing, stage-specific loss pattern.\r\n      A \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 fraction of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 sampled lost rows share the exact creation timestamp 2026-01-05T18:17:55.xxx, have null owner, null amount, and placeholder names like '\u2588\u2588\u2588', 'Self-hosted', 'SaaS' \u2014 signatures of a bulk backfill rather than deals actively worked and lost in the funnel.\r\n  [supported] The current open pipeline is bottlenecked at the presentation stage, which is where the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st share of live deal value currently sits without progressing.\r\n      \u2588\u2588% of open deals (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588) and a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 share of pipeline value are parked at presentationscheduled, while only \u2588 have reached contractsent, indicating the presentation-to-decision transition is the most crowded and least-converted step in the live pipeline today.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Add and start populating a 'stage_at_loss' (or equivalent last-active-stage) property on the deal object at the moment a deal is marked closed-lost, rather than overwriting stage with a terminal 'closedlost' value that destroys the funnel-position history.\r\n      why: Without this field, the exact question asked here \u2014 which stage loses the most deals by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and value \u2014 cannot be answered from HubSpot data at all; it can only be answered once loss events start recording where in the funnel they occurred.\r\n      [hubspot.search dd14c96f]\r\n  P\u2588 Investigate and, if confirmed as pure backfill, exclude or flag the ~\u2588\u2588-deal cluster created on 2026-01-05 with null owner/amount from loss-rate and win-rate reporting so the \u2588\u2588:\u2588 lost:won ratio is not \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 by a historical import.\r\n      why: Treating imported legacy \u2588\u2588\u2588/placeholder deals as live pipeline losses over\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s the current loss rate and could misdirect fixes toward a problem that is \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ly a data-migration artifact.\r\n      [hubspot.search dd14c96f]\r\n  P\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 sales-process attention on the presentation-to-decision transition, since \u2588\u2588% of live open pipeline value is currently parked at presentationscheduled versus only \u2588 deals at contractsent.\r\n      why: This is the one stage-level bottleneck the current data can actually support, using the open pipeline's live stage field as the best available proxy for where deals stall today.\r\n      [hubspot.pipeline 552c730a]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The closed-lost search was truncated at \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 matching rows, and the digest's own totals \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 only \u2588\u2588 of those \u2588\u2588\u2588 rows as having a non-null amount, so any total lost value figure quoted here is a floor, not the true total.\r\n  - Because the CRM never records the stage a deal was in immediately before being marked closed-lost, any future stage-of-loss analysis is impossible until that property is captured going forward \u2014 the gap is structural, not a one-off reporting limitation.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The sample of returned records confirms all show stage 'closedlost' with no prior-funnel-stage field, and total_matching=\u2588\u2588\u2588 matches the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 cited, though only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 records\r\n- findings[0].claims[0]: The evidence shows only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 records (truncated) and each shown record has stage 'closedlost' with no prior-stage field present, but this doesn't confirm all \u2588\u2588\u2588 records or p\r\n- findings[1].claims[1]: Won totals and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 match exactly, but the evidence doesn't \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 that only \u2588\u2588 of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 lost rows have a recorded amount (only truncated records are shown, not a full breakdown \r\n  - \u2588 causal claim(s) were withheld: a separate check of the evidence gathered, made without seeing this report, found that it does not support a definitive answer about cause. The evidence shows aggregate closed-won, open pipeline, and closed-lost deal lists but never breaks losses down by the stage at which they were lost, which is exactly what the question asks; without that \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ing and with the closed-lost list truncated to \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 rows, no stage-level cause or fix can be identified from this data. What would settle it: Stage-level breakdown of closed-lost deals (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed by the stage they were in prior to being marked closedlost), not just the aggregate closedlost list; Full record set for closed-lost deals rather than \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 truncated results; Historical stage-loss comparison across an earlier period to know if this distribution is a change or baseline; Deal history/timeline data showing which pipeline stage each lost deal was sitting in before loss. What remains describes wha\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The closed-lost deal search returned \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 total matching rows (truncated); totals derived from it, including the amount sum, cover only the returned/sampled rows and under\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 the true \u2588\u2588-month lost total.\r\n  - \u2588\u2588 of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 sampled closed-lost rows (and many more in the full \u2588\u2588\u2588) have no 'amount' value recorded at all, so lost deal value is under\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed wherever amount is null rather than genuinely zero.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  26c8926f  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2025-09-23..2026-09-23\r\n  552c730a  hubspot.pipeline  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?open=true\r\n  dd14c96f  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2025-09-23..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (131s wall, 129s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1      0.9    1%     0.9  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      4.1    3%     4.1  in 0 out 0\r\n  loop_model       3     41.7   32%    13.9  in 6 out 3,083 cached 24,829\r\n  loop_tools       2      1.8    1%     0.9  in 0 out 0\r\n  draft            1     65.2   50%    65.2  in 58,378 out 6,231\r\n  gate             1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  verify           1      9.5    7%     9.5  in 49,241 out 1,483\r\n  sufficiency      1      5.5    4%     5.5  in 4,069 out 277\r\n  unmeasured              2.0    2%\r\n  cache hit rate: 18%\r\n"]
